include/save_error_log_position.inc
# restart: --force_pqc=ON --tls-version=TLSv1.2
Server disables force_pqc when startup tls_version is TLSv1.2-only
SELECT @@GLOBAL.force_pqc, @@GLOBAL.tls_version;
@@GLOBAL.force_pqc	@@GLOBAL.tls_version
0	TLSv1.2
include/assert_error_log.inc [server: 1, pattern: force_pqc=ON requires TLSv1.3 with OpenSSL 3.5.0 or newer, but tls_version=TLSv1.2 disables TLSv1.3; setting force_pqc=OFF]
TLSv1.2 client is accepted after startup adjustment
Variable_name	Value
Ssl_version	TLSv1.2
# restart: --force_pqc=ON
Server reports force_pqc enabled after restart
SELECT @@GLOBAL.force_pqc;
@@GLOBAL.force_pqc
1
TLSv1.3 client negotiates a PQC key exchange
Variable_name	Value
Ssl_version	TLSv1.3
uses_pqc
1
TLSv1.3 session created under PQC resumes successfully
include/assert_grep.inc [TLSv1.3 PQC session is reused when force_pqc is enabled at startup]
TLSv1.2 client is rejected when force_pqc=ON
include/save_error_log_position.inc
# restart:
include/assert_error_log.inc [server: 1, pattern: TLS channel 'mysql_main' is not configured to require post-quantum key exchange algorithms; future TLS sessions may use a non-post-quantum key exchange algorithm because force_pqc is disabled]
TLSv1.2 client is accepted when force_pqc=OFF
Variable_name	Value
Ssl_version	TLSv1.2
SET @tls_kex_saved = @@GLOBAL.tls_kex;
SET @use_pqc_sign_saved = @@GLOBAL.use_pqc_sign;
Runtime validation rejects invalid main tls_kex
SET GLOBAL tls_kex = 'not_a_group';
ERROR 42000: Variable 'tls_kex' can't be set to the value of 'not_a_group'
Runtime validation rejects invalid main use_pqc_sign
SET GLOBAL use_pqc_sign = 'not_a_bool';
ERROR 42000: Variable 'use_pqc_sign' can't be set to the value of 'not_a_bool'
Client force-pqc rejects resumed non-PQC session data
SET GLOBAL tls_kex = 'X25519';
include/assert_grep.inc [non-PQC session data can resume without client force-pqc]
SET GLOBAL tls_kex = @tls_kex_saved;
Runtime enable clears the TLS session cache
SET GLOBAL force_pqc = ON;
Runtime validation rejects non-PQC main tls_kex when force_pqc=ON
SET GLOBAL tls_kex = 'X25519';
ERROR 42000: Variable 'tls_kex' can't be set to the value of 'X25519'
Server reports force_pqc enabled after runtime update
SELECT @@GLOBAL.force_pqc;
@@GLOBAL.force_pqc
1
TLSv1.3 session ticket captured before enable is rejected after runtime update
TLSv1.3 session created after runtime enable resumes successfully
include/assert_grep.inc [TLSv1.3 PQC session is reused after runtime force_pqc enable]
TLSv1.3 client negotiates a PQC key exchange after runtime update
Variable_name	Value
Ssl_version	TLSv1.3
uses_pqc
1
TLSv1.2 client is rejected after runtime update
SET @tls_version_saved = @@GLOBAL.tls_version;
include/save_error_log_position.inc
SET GLOBAL tls_version = 'TLSv1.2';
ALTER INSTANCE RELOAD TLS fails for force_pqc with TLSv1.2-only
ALTER INSTANCE RELOAD TLS;
ERROR HY000: Failed to set up SSL because of the following SSL library error: force_pqc requires TLSv1.3 with OpenSSL 3.5.0 or newer
TLSv1.3 client still negotiates a PQC key exchange after failed reload
Variable_name	Value
Ssl_version	TLSv1.3
uses_pqc
1
TLSv1.2 client is still rejected after failed reload
SET GLOBAL tls_version = @tls_version_saved;
ALTER INSTANCE RELOAD TLS;
SET GLOBAL force_pqc = OFF;
include/save_error_log_position.inc
ALTER INSTANCE RELOAD TLS;
include/assert_error_log.inc [server: 1, pattern: TLS channel 'mysql_main' is not configured to require post-quantum key exchange algorithms; future TLS sessions may use a non-post-quantum key exchange algorithm because force_pqc is disabled]
